## API Migration Mapping

### Core Processing → LibGDX Equivalents

| Processing API | LibGDX Equivalent | Complexity | Notes |
|---------------|-------------------|------------|-------|
| `PApplet` class | `ApplicationListener` | HIGH | Complete paradigm shift |
| `PVector` | `Vector3` | MEDIUM | Method name changes (mult→scl) |
| `draw()` | `render()` | HIGH | Lifecycle differences |
| `settings()` | `LwjglApplicationConfiguration` | MEDIUM | Config object instead |
| `setup()` | `create()` | LOW | Nearly 1:1 mapping |

### 3D Rendering APIs

| Processing | LibGDX | Implementation Strategy |
|-----------|--------|------------------------|
| `background(r,g,b)` | `Gdx.gl.glClearColor() + glClear()` | Direct OpenGL |
| `ortho()` | `camera = new OrthographicCamera()` | Camera object |
| `translate(x,y,z)` | `camera.translate()` or `modelInstance.transform.translate()` | Camera or model transform |
| `rotateX/Y/Z(angle)` | `camera.rotateAround()` or `transform.rotate()` | Transform API |
| `pushMatrix()/popMatrix()` | Manual matrix stack OR model hierarchy | Implement stack manually |
| `point(x,y,z)` | `ShapeRenderer.point()` or custom mesh | Use ShapeRenderer |
| `line(x1,y1,z1,x2,y2,z2)` | `ShapeRenderer.line()` | Use ShapeRenderer |
| `box(w,h,d)` | `ModelBuilder.createBox()` | Create model instances |
| `stroke(r,g,b)` | `shapeRenderer.setColor()` | Per-draw-call color |
| `strokeWeight(w)` | `Gdx.gl.glLineWidth()` | OpenGL call |
| `screenX/Y/Z(x,y,z)` | `camera.project(Vector3)` | Camera projection method |
| `text(str, x, y)` | `BitmapFont.draw()` with `SpriteBatch` | Separate text rendering |
| `applyMatrix()` | `transform.set(Matrix4)` | Direct matrix manipulation |

### Math & Utility APIs

| Processing | LibGDX | Notes |
|-----------|--------|-------|
| `PApplet.map(val, s1, e1, s2, e2)` | `MathUtils.map(val, s1, e1, s2, e2)` | Create custom utility |
| `PApplet.constrain(val, min, max)` | `MathUtils.clamp(val, min, max)` | Built-in |
| `PApplet.dist(x1,y1,x2,y2)` | `Vector2.dst(v1, v2)` | Use vector methods |
| `PApplet.floor(x)` | `MathUtils.floor(x)` | Built-in |
| `PApplet.sin/cos(x)` | `MathUtils.sin/cos(x)` | Built-in |
| `PApplet.noise(x,y,z)` | **CUSTOM IMPLEMENTATION** | Must implement Perlin noise |
| `PApplet.noiseDetail(lod, falloff)` | **CUSTOM IMPLEMENTATION** | Part of noise generator |

### Color APIs

| Processing | LibGDX | Notes |
|-----------|--------|-------|
| `color(r,g,b)` | `Color.toIntBits(r,g,b,a)` or `new Color(r,g,b,a)` | Float 0-1 vs int 0-255 |
| `colorMode(HSB)` | **CUSTOM IMPLEMENTATION** | LibGDX has no HSB mode |
| `red(color)` | `(color >> 16) & 0xFF` | Bit manipulation |
| `green(color)` | `(color >> 8) & 0xFF` | Bit manipulation |
| `blue(color)` | `color & 0xFF` | Bit manipulation |

### Image/Texture APIs

| Processing | LibGDX | Notes |
|-----------|--------|-------|
| `PImage` | `Texture` or `Pixmap` | Use Texture for display, Pixmap for pixels |
| `loadImage(path)` | `new Texture(Gdx.files.internal(path))` | File handle API |
| `image.pixels[]` | `pixmap.getPixel(x, y)` | Per-pixel access |

### Event APIs

| Processing | LibGDX | Notes |
|-----------|--------|-------|
| `mousePressed()` method | `InputProcessor.touchDown()` | Interface implementation |
| `keyPressed()` method | `InputProcessor.keyDown()` | Interface implementation |
| `mouseX/mouseY` fields | `Gdx.input.getX()/getY()` | Polling instead of fields |

