## Phased Migration Plan

### Phase 0: Pre-Migration (CRITICAL - DO FIRST)

**Duration**: 20-30 complexity units
**Purpose**: Risk mitigation and validation
**Status**: Not Started

#### P0.1: Create Proof of Concept
**Effort**: HIGH (15-20 units)
**Dependencies**: None

**Description**:
Implement ONE simple clip (PerlinNoiseClip) in LibGDX as standalone test project. This validates:
- LibGDX can render point clouds correctly
- Perlin noise can be matched
- Performance is acceptable
- Visual output matches Processing

**Acceptance Criteria**:
- [ ] Standalone LibGDX project created
- [ ] PerlinNoiseClip ported to LibGDX APIs
- [ ] Perlin noise implementation passes comparison tests
- [ ] Side-by-side screenshot comparison with Processing version
- [ ] Performance benchmarked (frame rate, memory)
- [ ] Differences documented and evaluated
- [ ] GO/NO-GO decision made based on POC results

**Technical Notes**:
- Use same noise seed for comparison
- Capture 100+ frames from both versions
- Use image diff tools to validate visual parity
- If any significant differences found, STOP and re-evaluate

**Risk**: If POC fails or shows unacceptable differences, entire migration approach needs reconsideration.

#### P0.2: Extract Rendering Interfaces
**Effort**: MEDIUM (8-12 units)
**Dependencies**: None (can be done in parallel with P0.1)

**Description**:
Refactor current Processing code to separate business logic from rendering. Create interfaces that both Processing and LibGDX can implement.

**Acceptance Criteria**:
- [ ] `IRenderer` interface created with draw methods
- [ ] OnScreen.java refactored to implement IRenderer
- [ ] TesseractMain uses IRenderer instead of direct OnScreen
- [ ] Clip classes use abstract vector/math APIs where possible
- [ ] All tests still pass with refactored code
- [ ] No functionality changes, only structure

**Technical Notes**:
```java
public interface IRenderer {
    void initialize();
    void render();
    void drawPoint(float x, float y, float z, int r, int g, int b);
    void drawLine(float x1, float y1, float z1, float x2, float y2, float z2);
    void drawText(String text, float x, float y);
    void setCamera(float rotX, float rotY);
    Vector3 project(float x, float y, float z);
}
```

**Risk**: Low - This improves architecture regardless of migration decision.

