#### P1.2: Utility Classes
**Effort**: MEDIUM (8-12 units)
**Dependencies**: None

**Description**:
Create LibGDX-based utility classes to replace Processing static methods. These are used throughout the codebase.

**Acceptance Criteria**:
- [ ] `TesseractMathUtils.java` created with map, constrain, dist methods
- [ ] `ProcessingPerlinNoise.java` created with noise() and noiseDetail()
- [ ] `ColorUtils.java` created for RGB/HSB conversion
- [ ] Unit tests for all utility methods
- [ ] Output matches Processing for 1000+ test cases
- [ ] Perlin noise specifically validated against Processing's output

**Technical Notes**:
```java
public class TesseractMathUtils {
    public static float map(float value, float start1, float stop1, float start2, float stop2) {
        return start2 + (stop2 - start2) * ((value - start1) / (stop1 - start1));
    }

    public static float constrain(float value, float min, float max) {
        return MathUtils.clamp(value, min, max);
    }

    public static float dist(float x1, float y1, float x2, float y2) {
        return Vector2.dst(x1, y1, x2, y2);
    }
}

public class ColorUtils {
    // HSB to RGB conversion
    public static int colorHSB(float h, float s, float b) {
        // Implement HSB→RGB algorithm matching Processing
    }

    // RGB color creation
    public static int colorRGB(int r, int g, int b) {
        return ((0xFF << 24) | (r << 16) | (g << 8) | b);
    }
}
```

**Files**:
- New: `src/main/util/TesseractMathUtils.java`
- New: `src/main/util/ProcessingPerlinNoise.java`
- New: `src/main/util/ColorUtils.java`
- New: `src/test/util/UtilityClassesTest.groovy`

