### Phase 2: 3D Rendering System

**Duration**: 60-80 complexity units
**Purpose**: Replace Processing's immediate-mode rendering with LibGDX
**Status**: Not Started
**Prerequisites**: Phase 1 complete

#### P2.1: Camera System
**Effort**: HIGH (12-16 units)
**Dependencies**: P1.4 (application lifecycle), P1.5 (input handling)

**Description**:
Implement LibGDX camera to replace Processing's automatic projection. Support orthographic projection and mouse-based rotation matching OnScreen.java behavior.

**Acceptance Criteria**:
- [ ] `TesseractCamera.java` created managing OrthographicCamera
- [ ] Orthographic projection configured matching Processing's ortho()
- [ ] Mouse drag rotation working (matching OnScreen.java easing)
- [ ] Camera.project() method replaces screenX/screenY
- [ ] Camera positioned and oriented correctly
- [ ] View frustum configured for stage bounding box
- [ ] Manual testing confirms camera behavior matches Processing

**Technical Notes**:
```java
public class TesseractCamera {
    private OrthographicCamera camera;
    private float xrot, yrot;
    private float targetXrot, targetYrot;
    private Vector3 tmpVec = new Vector3();

    public TesseractCamera(int viewportWidth, int viewportHeight) {
        camera = new OrthographicCamera(viewportWidth, viewportHeight);
        camera.near = 1f;
        camera.far = 10000f;
        camera.position.set(0, 0, 500);
        camera.lookAt(0, 0, 0);
        camera.update();
    }

    public void update(float deltaTime) {
        // Implement easing like OnScreen.java
        float diff = xrot - targetXrot;
        if (Math.abs(diff) > 0.01f) {
            xrot -= diff / 6.0f;
        }
        // ... same for yrot

        camera.direction.set(0, 0, -1);
        camera.up.set(0, 1, 0);
        camera.rotateAround(Vector3.Zero, new Vector3(1,0,0), xrot);
        camera.rotateAround(Vector3.Zero, new Vector3(0,1,0), yrot);
        camera.update();
    }

    public Vector2 project(float x, float y, float z) {
        tmpVec.set(x, y, z);
        camera.project(tmpVec);
        return new Vector2(tmpVec.x, tmpVec.y);
    }
}
```

**File**: New `src/main/rendering/TesseractCamera.java`

#### P2.2: Shape Renderer for Points/Lines
**Effort**: HIGH (12-16 units)
