**Technical Notes**:
```java
public class TesseractShapeRenderer {
    private ShapeRenderer shapeRenderer;
    private TesseractCamera camera;

    public void begin() {
        shapeRenderer.begin(ShapeRenderer.ShapeType.Point);
        shapeRenderer.setProjectionMatrix(camera.getCamera().combined);
    }

    public void drawPoint(float x, float y, float z, Color color) {
        shapeRenderer.setColor(color);
        shapeRenderer.point(x, y, z);
    }

    public void drawLine(float x1, float y1, float z1, float x2, float y2, float z2, Color color) {
        shapeRenderer.setColor(color);
        shapeRenderer.line(x1, y1, z1, x2, y2, z2);
    }

    public void end() {
        shapeRenderer.end();
    }
}
```

**File**: New `src/main/rendering/TesseractShapeRenderer.java`

#### P2.3: Renderer Implementation
**Effort**: VERY HIGH (20-30 units)
**Dependencies**: P2.1 (camera), P2.2 (shape renderer)

**Description**:
Create complete rendering system to replace OnScreen.java. Handle all 3D visualization including nodes, axes, bounding box, text, and framerate display.

**Acceptance Criteria**:
- [ ] `TesseractRenderer.java` created implementing IRenderer interface
- [ ] All OnScreen.java drawing logic ported
- [ ] Axes drawing functional (red/green/blue lines)
- [ ] Bounding box drawing functional
- [ ] Node point cloud rendering functional with colors
- [ ] Text rendering working (FPS, status messages)
- [ ] Camera rotation and positioning matching OnScreen.java
- [ ] Screen projection for node.screenX/Y working
- [ ] Performance at 30fps with full stage
- [ ] Side-by-side visual comparison with Processing version passes

**Technical Notes**:
```java
public class TesseractRenderer implements IRenderer {
    private TesseractCamera camera;
    private TesseractShapeRenderer shapeRenderer;
    private SpriteBatch spriteBatch;
    private BitmapFont font;
    private boolean drawingEnabled = true;

    @Override
    public void render(Node[] nodes) {
        Gdx.gl.glClearColor(20f/255f, 20f/255f, 20f/255f, 1f);
        Gdx.gl.glClear(GL20.GL_COLOR_BUFFER_BIT | GL20.GL_DEPTH_BUFFER_BIT);
        Gdx.gl.glEnable(GL20.GL_DEPTH_TEST);

        camera.update(Gdx.graphics.getDeltaTime());

        if (!drawingEnabled) {
            drawFramerate();
            return;
        }

        shapeRenderer.begin();

        // Draw axes
        drawAxes(600);

        // Draw bounding box
        drawBoundingBox(stage);

        // Draw all nodes as points
        for (Node node : nodes) {
            Color color = new Color(node.r/255f, node.g/255f, node.b/255f, 1f);
            shapeRenderer.drawPoint(node.x, node.y, node.z, color);

            // Update screen coordinates
            Vector2 screenPos = camera.project(node.x, node.y, node.z);
            node.screenX = screenPos.x;
            node.screenY = screenPos.y;
        }

        shapeRenderer.end();

        drawFramerate();
    }

    private void drawFramerate() {
        spriteBatch.begin();
        font.draw(spriteBatch, "FPS " + Gdx.graphics.getFramesPerSecond(),
                  Gdx.graphics.getWidth() - 60, 20);
        spriteBatch.end();
    }
}
```

**File**: New `src/main/rendering/TesseractRenderer.java`

#### P2.4: Matrix Transformation System
**Effort**: MEDIUM (8-12 units)
**Dependencies**: P2.3 (renderer)

**Description**:
Implement matrix stack and custom rotation (rotateXYZ) to replace Processing's pushMatrix/popMatrix and applyMatrix.

**Acceptance Criteria**:
- [ ] Manual matrix stack implemented
- [ ] pushMatrix()/popMatrix() equivalent methods working
- [ ] rotateXYZ() custom rotation for Tesseract cube working
- [ ] Matrix transformations applied correctly to camera/models
- [ ] Tesseract cube orientation matches Processing output
- [ ] No matrix leaks or stack issues

**Technical Notes**:
```java
public class MatrixStack {
    private Array<Matrix4> stack = new Array<>();
    private Matrix4 current = new Matrix4();

    public void pushMatrix() {
        stack.add(current.cpy());
    }

    public void popMatrix() {
        if (stack.size > 0) {
            current.set(stack.pop());
        }
    }

    public void rotateXYZ(float xx, float yy, float zz) {
        float cx = MathUtils.cos(xx);
        float cy = MathUtils.cos(yy);
        float cz = MathUtils.cos(zz);
        float sx = MathUtils.sin(xx);
        float sy = MathUtils.sin(yy);
        float sz = MathUtils.sin(zz);

        Matrix4 rotMat = new Matrix4();
        // Set matrix values matching OnScreen.java rotateXYZ
        current.mul(rotMat);
    }
}
```

**File**: New `src/main/rendering/MatrixStack.java`

