#### P3.2: PerlinNoiseClip Migration
**Effort**: MEDIUM (8-12 units)
**Dependencies**: P3.1 (abstract clip), P1.2 (perlin noise implementation)

**Description**:
Port PerlinNoiseClip to use LibGDX utilities. This is the POC clip, so should be straightforward if Phase 0 POC succeeded.

**Acceptance Criteria**:
- [ ] All Processing API calls removed
- [ ] Uses ProcessingPerlinNoise for noise generation
- [ ] Uses ColorUtils for color operations
- [ ] Uses TesseractMathUtils for map/floor
- [ ] Visual output matches Processing version pixel-perfect
- [ ] Performance acceptable
- [ ] Unit tests for noise calculation

**Technical Notes**:
```java
// Before (Processing)
float n = _myMain.noise(nX, nY, _theta);
int c = _myMain.color(r, g, b);

// After (LibGDX)
float n = ProcessingPerlinNoise.noise(nX, nY, _theta);
int c = ColorUtils.colorRGB(r, g, b);
```

